The two M0 pilots establish project feasibility and proof effort, not permission to replace the ten-contract scope by two lemmas. Public targets must compile without `sorry`, `admit` or unapproved project axioms; retain `#print axioms` output and allow only the recorded foundations of the pinned environment. F1 assumes moment identities for a selected transition basis: numerical THB patch tests still have to establish that the implementation satisfies them. A noncritical deferral requires an explicit ADR naming the missing theorem, reason, numerical substitute and revisit milestone.

Report four distinct evidence classes: kernel-checked exact-arithmetic contracts, independent numerical-reference results, C++/CUDA parity and runtime invariants, and real-device end-to-end quality/performance. None replaces another. The contracts do not prove Navier–Stokes, total simulation stability, IEEE bounds, memory safety, collision geometry or reconstructed topology. An independent Python operator reference and bounded portions of F5 and F8 are implemented. Their four Lean targets were also checked by an experimental independent checker; the full ten families and production/CUDA gates remain outstanding.

== Product constraints and measured choices <sec-open>
Product decisions are recorded:
- *Scene*: sloping beach, Stokes swell, fixed camera (@sec-scope). *D1*: sheets below $Delta x_min$ are carried by the mesh only. *D2*: `sim/` holds band particles every frame and all particles at checkpoints.
- *D3*: one MAC grid for all continua. *D4*: foam projected in Geometry Nodes; Mesh never reads `whitewater/`. *D5*: physical low-Mach gas with few parameters.
- *D6*: fractional viscosity step, coupled Stokes only if the planar-extension test requires it. *D7*: two-way rigid bodies at M6. *D8*: Ryzen 7 9700X, 64 GB, 3 TB.
- *D9*: adaptivity is a firm objective; at most six hours is tolerated temporarily without it, and an AG-MPM/GIMP alternative is tried before any abandonment. Supersonic flow is not implemented but kept addable. *D10*: unresolved trapped air may collapse before M4; resolved cavities receive physical pressure at M4. Finite-c liquid is a design option with physical grid pressure history.
What remains is settled by measurement, not by product decision: the exact flow-map gate thresholds (@sec-flowmap), validation of weak liquid compressibility (@sec-weak, M4), and builder values.

== Evidence boundaries
No FluidiTy simulation result is reported here; source-inspection facts and cited platform timings are explicitly attributed. The design equations are contracts, and the budgets (three hours, or six without adaptivity; 11 GB; the 4.8 GB estimate) are acceptance objectives and estimates, not CUDA results. The largest risks are a 3D THB-MPM MAC basis on GPU (not validated by the cited sources; go/no-go after the uniform baseline, with the D9 fallback), a tracked mesh combined with multiresolution (integration unvalidated), memory bandwidth, the cost of fixed-point P2G, and reading caches in Blender without Python. Validation proceeds milestone by milestone with exit criteria measured on the target GPU. The storage schema, optional modules and memory examples are engineering choices of this project; they should not be attributed as a single published algorithm to any reference below.

